SRC/hanoi -- hanoi and hanoimod, as built for OS-9/68000=========================================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.misc carried it.  hanoi.c buildsunchanged.  hanoimod.c differs in one line, under #ifdef OSK: it allocated`number' BYTES for an array of number+1 ints, so every move wrote past theend of the block; it now allocates (number + 1) * sizeof(int).  `hanoimod 10'prints its 4092 lines and exits 0.